00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.970
I didn't mean anything by that. I was just kidding.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:23.640
Fine. I'm not going to give you any of Dad's special New Year's Eve dishes.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.510
Oh, no, don't rule. I mean, you're kidding, aren't you?

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.970
It just didn't come out the right way, that's...

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:36.680
I meant to say that you look very cute, and the color of the outfit brings out your eyes, and it really suits you.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.580
And please forgive me, Sakura.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.060
Do you really think this outfit suits me?

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:47.320
Oh, yeah. It suits you better than anything you've ever worn before, and I am not just saying that.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.290
Okay, that's enough, Kiro. I'll bring you some of that food later on, all right?

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:58.360
Oh, thank goodness. I love your dad's New Year's dishes.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.000
So, how do I hold...

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:17.290
All right, Squirt.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.360
Calling me Squirt!

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.490
Hey, Sakura and Tori. Happy New Year, you two.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.370
Thanks. Happy New Year to you, too.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.200
That outfit looks great on you, Sakura.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.100
You really think so?

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:39.800
I sure do. And here are your New Year's cards.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:41.780
Wow! Thank you very much, Dad.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:43.460
You're very welcome.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.400
Just give me a couple minutes, okay?

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.960
I have to wrap up a little work,

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:50.540
and then we'll make our first trip of the year to the shrine.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:52.450
Hey!

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:10.160
I got from everybody oh here's one from Lee what are you talking about that bratty kid he is not

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:17.600
bratty okay and his name is Lee oh just call him the brat you know we is a really nice kid and if

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:25.240
you took the time to notice he always helps me out when I really need him yeah that's what bugs me

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.260
about him what did you say something nothing

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:30.600
Let's go.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.480
Okay, kids, shall we be on our way?

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:44.220
Tell me then, Sakura, have you thought about what you're going to wish for this year?

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.130
Who, me?

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.660
Well, I wish my math marks would be higher next term.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.880
Then I wish I could get better at the baton.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:55.620
Oh, and I also wish that Madison will win the citywide choir competition coming up.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.300
Hope you brought enough coins to offer.

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:12.950
He said he was gonna meet us here at the shrine?

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:13.510
Yeah.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.480
It's not usually like Julian to be as late as this, is it, Tori?

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:23.570
I'm gonna go drop by Julian's house to see if he's there still.

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:24.770
Uh, go on without me.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.000
Say hi to him for us, okay?

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:28.100
Sure.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.700
Tori said he's been late for school a lot, too.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.060
I wonder what's going on with Julian.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.180
It's Mousin!

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:14.520
first wish this year Madison I wish that we'd be friends forever come over here

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:28.100
and I'll take your picture the girls look great today okay are you ready say cheese

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.420
Boy, I was sure nervous.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:38.020
I'm sure the pictures will turn out just fine.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.800
My mom takes great pictures.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:43.600
Come over to our house one day soon, okay?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:44.880
Okay.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.920
Well then, I guess I'd better be going home, too.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.280
I have to start making the New Year's dinner.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:51.780
Help out, too.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.120
You and Tori helped prepare some of the dishes yesterday.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.840
There's nothing left for you to do.

00:05:57.420 --> 00:05:59.400
Why don't you stay out a little longer with Madison?

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:00.680
Sure.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:10.520
Late, okay?

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:18.910
We'll get our fortunes?

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:19.490
Sure.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.690
Excuse me, we would like to get our fortunes, please.

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.530
Sure, just help yourselves.

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.250
Eli, it's you!

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.960
So, what are you doing here today?

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:43.890
Well, you see, I heard they needed volunteers to help out today, so here I am.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.020
Oh, oh, that's right.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:48.100
Miss Mackenzie's away teaching in England.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.200
Uh, well, you sure surprised me.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.220
Do you know the people who run this shrine?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.040
Just one of them.

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:56.720
Huh?

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.820
Okay, time for you two to get your fortunes.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:02.970
Come on, come on!

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:09.370
Got number 75, got 42.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.840
Okay, I'll be right back.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:18.320
It's a good one.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.840
Wait to see.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:29.150
Thanks so much for waiting. This one is yours, Madison.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:30.760
Thanks, Eli.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.380
And this one is yours, Sakura.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:34.350
Thanks.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.830
Oh, what is it?

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:38.840
I got a good one.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.490
All your dreams will come true.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:42.840
What's yours?

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.500
Oh, uh, uh-huh?

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:48.600
Truth can be found in your first dream of the year.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:53.700
Mysterious, isn't it?

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:55.890
Is there something the matter?

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.310
Well, the part about good luck is missing from this fortune.

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:02.510
That's a very special fortune you have there.

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:03.930
It's special.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:24.700
Hmm. How special that fortune is, Sekiro.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:44.910
Ju- Julian!

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.190
Hi, Tori.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:03.400
What happened to you?

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.700
I just got really tired all of a sudden.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:08.220
Huh?

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:10.330
I'm okay now.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.880
So what are you doing here, anyway?

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.480
What are you talking about?

00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:17.270
You're the one who said you wanted to come to the shrine with us.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:20.330
I mean, we waited and waited and you just never showed up.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:22.080
Sorry about that.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:23.730
Oh, that's alright.

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:27.130
If we hurry, we can still catch up to Sakura and the others at the shrine.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:29.130
Oh, hey, Julian, what's wrong?

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.790
Sorry, I'm just so exhausted lately.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:07.580
I see. Some friends from school have come to visit.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:11.490
Hi, Wei. We'd like to wish you a happy new year.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:15.720
Thank you very much. Happy new year to you both as well.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:18.920
You are the first visitors to our home this year.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.900
Please, come on in. I'll prepare some tea.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:24.380
We're not interrupting, are we?

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:27.290
Don't even think of it. Isn't that right, Leigh?

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:29.870
Uh, that's right. Please.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:37.790
come in won't you okay we'll stay for tea boy something smells really good looks

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:51.920
very much way very welcome hey this dessert looks so amazing delicious did

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:55.920
you make these desserts way no master Lee made them

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:09.340
New Year's Feast was fantastic, and this dessert is delicious, too!

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.580
This is gonna be a great year!

